## Style notes for the eventual full text

- Single Markdown file (Bikeshed `.bs` source or IETF Markdown), rendered to one HTML page.
- Each numeric heading anchors a stable URL fragment (`#section-8-3-2`) for cross-reference from CMS / ONC programs.
- Every `SHALL` / `SHOULD` / `MAY` line annotated with the conformance class it binds (verifier / wallet / verifier-side validator).
- Examples blocks marked `(EX)` and excluded from normative text.
- Each binding section ends with a "Verifier MUST do exactly the following" checklist and a "Wallet MUST do exactly the following" checklist so a certification suite can be written one-to-one against the spec.
- Platform-specific machinery (e.g., Android Credential Manager matchers, iOS wallet APIs) appears only in §15 implementation notes; protocol-level requirements MUST be platform-neutral.
